\p
\v 29 When the \sc Lord\sc* \w thy God| strong="H430" \w* [shall cut off]{strong=“H3772” x-morph=“strongMorph: \sc Th\sc*8686”} \w the nations| strong="H1471" \w* \w from before| strong="H6440" \w* [thee, whither thou goest]{strong=“H935” x-morph=“strongMorph: \sc Th\sc*8802”} [to possess]{strong=“H3423” x-morph=“strongMorph: \sc Th\sc*8800”} [them, and thou succeedest]{strong=“H3423” x-morph=“strongMorph: \sc Th\sc*8804”} [them, and dwellest]{strong=“H3427” x-morph=“strongMorph: \sc Th\sc*8804”} \w in their land| strong="H776" \w*;\f + \fr 12:29 \ft succeedest…: Heb. inheritest, or, possessest them \f* 
